                "headline": "Flood Watch issued November 12 at 2:12AM PST until November 15 at 4:00AM PST by NWS Seattle WA",
                "description": "* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is possible.\n\n* WHERE...A portion of northwest Washington, including the following\ncounty, Mason.\n\n* WHEN...From late tonight through late Saturday night.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Three to four and a half inches of rain is forecast for the south\nslopes of the Olympics between early Friday and early Sunday with\nsnow levels of 5500 to 6500 feet. The combination of heavy rain\nand relatively high snow levels could push the Skokomish River\nnear Potlatch above flood stage.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
                "instruction": "You should monitor later forecasts and be alert for possible Flood\nWarnings. Those living in areas prone to flooding should be prepared\nto take action should flooding develop.",
